<article class="env-lemma" id="0BY9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BY9">Lemma <span data-tag="0BY9">53.8.2</span>.</a> Let $k'/k$ be a field extension. Let $X$ be a proper scheme over $k$ having dimension $1$ and $H^0(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) = k$. Then $X_{k'}$ is a proper scheme over $k'$ having dimension $1$ and $H^0(X_{k'}, \mathcal{O}_{X_{k'}}) = k'$. Moreover the genus of $X_{k'}$ is equal to the genus of $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The dimension of $X_{k'}$ is $1$ for example by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FY" data-tag="02FY">29.29.3</a>. The morphism $X_{k'} \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(k')$ is proper by Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/01W4" data-tag="01W4">29.42.5</a>. The equality $H^0(X_{k'}, \mathcal{O}_{X_{k'}}) = k'$ follows from Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/02KH" data-tag="02KH">30.5.2</a>. The equality of the genus follows from the same lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>